==============================================================================
Code ported from BIMCraft
==============================================================================

crates/world/src/skeleton.rs is ported from BIMCraft
(https://github.com/IPedrax/bimcraft), crates/core/src/skeleton.rs and the
vector type and three helpers it uses from crates/core/src/geom.rs, at commit
f202abd85d1cf165325e2f7b250da0b5e51f5b71. BIMCraft is licensed MIT OR
Apache-2.0; the code is used here under the MIT license. The file's header
states that it is ported and lists what was changed.

crates/ifc/src/step.rs is ported from the same project at the same commit,
crates/core/src/step.rs (the reader of the STEP file IFC models are written
in), under the same license. Its header lists the one change made to it.

The building model is ported from the same project at the same commit, under
the same license:

  crates/world/src/building/model.rs    from crates/core/src/model.rs and
                                        crates/core/src/family.rs
  crates/world/src/building/walls.rs    from crates/core/src/walls.rs
  crates/world/src/building/runs.rs     from crates/core/src/runs.rs
  crates/world/src/building/network.rs  from crates/core/src/network.rs
  crates/world/src/building/rooms.rs    from crates/core/src/geom.rs,
                                        crates/core/src/rooms.rs and
                                        crates/core/src/model.rs
  crates/world/src/building/forms.rs    from crates/core/src/family.rs (the
                                        forms of ten families of its library)
  crates/world/src/building/framing.rs  from crates/core/src/timber.rs (the
                                        layout of a wall's frame)
  crates/world/src/building.rs          five small items from
                                        crates/core/src/model.rs and
                                        crates/core/src/view3d.rs; the rest of
                                        the file is this project's own

The plan set's page of line work and its PDF are ported from the same project at
the same commit, under the same license:

  crates/world/src/paper/mod.rs         from crates/core/src/render.rs (the
                                        display list: fills and lines)
  crates/world/src/paper/font.rs        from crates/core/src/font.rs (the
                                        lettering of strokes)
  crates/world/src/paper/pen.rs         from crates/core/src/pen.rs (the pens)
  crates/world/src/paper/size.rs        from crates/core/src/model.rs (paper
                                        sizes) and crates/core/src/units.rs
                                        (the scale's wording)
  crates/world/src/paper/cut.rs         from crates/core/src/render.rs (the
                                        wall-cut pass: joined walls)
  crates/world/src/paper/pdf.rs         from crates/core/src/pdf.rs (the PDF
                                        written by hand)

What draws and edits the building is ported from the same project at the same
commit, under the same license:

  crates/world/src/editing/history.rs   from crates/core/src/engine.rs
  crates/world/src/editing/snap.rs      from crates/core/src/snap.rs and
                                        crates/core/src/geom.rs
  crates/world/src/editing.rs           the verbs' rules, from
                                        crates/core/src/commands.rs,
                                        crates/core/src/draw.rs and
                                        crates/core/src/engine.rs; the file is
                                        otherwise this project's own
  crates/world/src/editing/join.rs      the rule for cutting a run in two, from
                                        split in crates/core/src/commands.rs;
                                        the rest of the file is this project's
                                        own
  crates/world/src/editing/stretch.rs   what a moved wall does at a joint, from
                                        relocate and move_elements in
                                        crates/core/src/commands.rs; the rest of
                                        the file is this project's own
  crates/world/src/editing/carry.rs     a line of points moved to its side, corners
                                        where the moved stretches meet, from
                                        offset_poly in crates/core/src/draw.rs and
                                        offset in crates/core/src/stairs.rs; the
                                        sharp-corner rule is this project's own

Each file's header states what is ported and lists what was changed. PORTMAP.md
names, for every public item of the building model, the BIMCraft file and line
it came from, or that it is this project's own and how that was checked.

