==============================================================================
Method ported from Cloud2BIM
==============================================================================

crates/plans/src/found_189.rs (the scan's walls found by the points near the
ceiling, `plumbline find-walls ... --by-ceiling`) follows the method of
Cloud2BIM (https://github.com/VaclavNezerka/Cloud2BIM, at its master branch as
read on 2026-11-23: LICENSE, README.md, config.yaml, cloud2entities.py and
aux_functions.py; the paper is arXiv 2503.11498). The order of work and the
measures its paper's parameter table states are ported: the points in the top
tenth of the height, laid on the plan as a density picture and closed, the
outlines of what is there, made straight by Douglas and Peucker, pieces on one
line merged within 3 degrees, opposite parallel faces paired into a wall, the
longest wall's direction taken as the axis, the ends carried to meet within half
the greatest thickness, and each wall's own face read for openings. The code is
written here in Rust from that description; no line of the Python is copied and
none of it is linked. Cloud2BIM is licensed MIT:

